Title: Guard askSDTLaunch's confirmEx call against a throwing host surface
Created: 2026-09-08
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-08T18:15Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Found by the red-team perspective of `/review-pr` on PR #481
(tickets/0742), which replaced the sitter's `Services.prompt.confirm(...)`
launch-prompt call with `Services.prompt.confirmEx(...)` reading
`BUTTON_POS_0`, `BUTTON_POS_1`, and `BUTTON_TITLE_IS_STRING` off
`Services.prompt` and combining them into an arithmetic bitmask
(`plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js`, `askSDTLaunch`).

Neither the old 3-argument `confirm()` call nor the new 9-argument
`confirmEx()` call is wrapped in try/catch. This is not a regression this
PR introduced — the old code had the same absence — but the surface that
can throw grew: four property reads feeding arithmetic, versus none
before, and `confirmEx`'s XPCOM `unsigned long` argument coercion can
throw on a non-finite value if any of the three `BUTTON_*` constants is
undefined on a given host.

If that happens, the throw is uncaught inside `initialize()` (an async
function), propagates as a rejected promise to `startup()`'s
`.catch(error => Zotero.logError(error))`, and leaves the plugin in a
state where `sitter` exists but `alive` is never set true, the toolbar
button and window never appear, and `armSDTSitter`/`disarmSDTSitter`
never run. Net effect: total, silent (console-only) non-activation — not
"indexing runs while the UI says off," but a plugin that never visibly
starts, with no user-facing signal beyond the Zotero error console.

The PR's own body already flagged this exact host surface as unverified:
"`tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` warns that no Zotero install was found, so the
host surface this diff newly names — `Services.prompt.confirmEx` and the
`BUTTON_*` constants — went unverified on this machine. Worth a live
check before release." This ticket is the live-check-and-harden half of
that admission.

## Relevant files

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` — `askSDTLaunch` (the confirmEx call
  and the `BUTTON_*` bitmask), and its caller in `initialize()`
- `tests/sdt_sitter_zotero_mock.mjs` — the `Services.prompt` mock; its
  `confirmEx` and `BUTTON_*` are hardcoded present and never throw, so no
  existing test exercises this path
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` — the pref-handling tests (`readSDTSwitch`
  coverage) that establish the sibling pattern: a hostile/throwing host
  input is read defensively and falls back to a safe default, never left
  to propagate

## Actions

1. On a real Zotero install, confirm `Services.prompt.BUTTON_POS_0`,
   `BUTTON_POS_1`, and `BUTTON_TITLE_IS_STRING` are present and that
   `confirmEx` accepts the 9-argument call as written (the live check the
   PR body asked for).
2. Wrap the bitmask computation and the `confirmEx` call in `askSDTLaunch`
   with a try/catch, matching the defensive idiom already used by
   `readSDTSwitch`/`writeSDTSwitch` for the pref. On catch, fail closed to
   "never answered" (return `null`/treat as declined) rather than letting
   the throw propagate into `initialize()`'s promise chain, and emit a
   diagnosable journal/error event so the failure is visible somewhere
   other than the Zotero error console.
3. Add a driven test in `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs` or
   `sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs` that makes the mock's `confirmEx` throw (or one
   of the `BUTTON_*` properties `undefined`) and asserts the plugin still
   reaches a visible, non-crashed state (toolbar + window present, phase
   readable) rather than silent non-activation.

## Test

Red step: a test that sets the mock's `Services.prompt.confirmEx` to
throw (or deletes `BUTTON_POS_0`) before `startup()`, then asserts the
toolbar button and window exist afterward. This fails against the
current code (no try/catch) and should pass once action 2 lands.

## Verification

- [ ] Live check on real Zotero confirms the three `BUTTON_*` constants
      and the 9-arg `confirmEx` signature (action 1)
- [ ] `askSDTLaunch` cannot propagate an uncaught throw into `initialize()`
- [ ] New driven test in the .mjs suite reddens against the pre-fix code
      and passes after the fix
- [ ] `make check` green

## Invariants

- No change to the tri-state pref semantics or the ordering (ask before
  `alive = true` and before toolbar install) ticket 0742 established.
- A failure here must still fail closed (no silent indexing), matching
  the existing `readSDTSwitch` failure mode.

## Exit criteria

`askSDTLaunch` cannot crash `initialize()` on a host where any of the
`BUTTON_*` constants is absent or `confirmEx` throws; the live-Zotero
check the PR body asked for has been run at least once; a driven test
guards the fix.

